The cleanup of `SSHConsoleConn` ([ref](https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-mgmt/blob/99b28c4f2072cead6ba6fff48821395eae75eda6/tests/common/connections/ssh_console_conn.py#L192)) writes `exit`. `e`, when written to at GRUB menu, enters the GRUB edit mode directly which is unexpected.

As part of the `netmiko` framework, the cleanup can be triggered by many ways. In my limited experience, this is typically triggered by an EOF exception during a console read while the reboot is happening. I think the cleanup is called correctly but should not blindly write `exit` to the console. In #24288 , the proposal is to first check that the console is likely at the SONiC prompt (which is the original intent based on the comment there).

@yxieca I have added this to the PR description (and also in #24288). Thank you for checking.
